  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe problem requires minimizing the maximum overlap integral for a step function under integral constraints. We use the initial solution as a structured starting point and employ a gradient-based approach with local refinement.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n- Variables: h \u2208 \u211d^{n_points} with h_i \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h = n_points / 2\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k (\u222bh(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx) \n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, \u2211h = n_points / 2\n- Initialization: Use initial_h_values as base, scaled and perturbed to generate starting populations.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\na. Initialization:\n   - Use initial_h_values if available. If not, generate h with uniform samples in [0.4, 0.6] and scale to meet sum constraint.\n\nb. Coordinate-wise Optimization:\n   - For each h_i, compute the optimal value while keeping others fixed.\n   - Update h_i to minimize the maximum overlap at each step.\n\nc. Constraint Handling:\n   - After updates, clamp h_i to [0, 1] and scale to ensure \u2211h = n_points / 2.\n\nd. Local Refinement:\n   - Apply SLSQP periodically on the best solution to refine.\n\ne. Termination:\n   - Continue until time budget is exhausted, evaluate best solution using exact objective.\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n- Resolution: n_points = 70\n- Population Size: 100\n- Gradient Tolerance: 1e-6\n- Mutation Factor: 0.85\n- Crossover Probability: 0.95\n- Periodic Refinement: After 100 iterations\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n- Time Allocation: 1100s with checks every 30s\n- Fallback: Maintain best solution found; return if time limit reached\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n- Ensure h_i \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h = n_points / 2\n- Validate C\u2085 using exact evaluator\n- Return best h, C5, n_points",
